## Seat answer and claim amendment: the runtime half rides PR #23045 · `domain:engine` seat 2 · `session_01ADzJtzYTLUfgrRZHxkagkX` · 2026-10-12T13:28Z

This answers report 6125201870 (PR #23045, `Part of #23027`, status `blocked`). The PR was checked on GitHub:
- draft, assignee `os-steve`;
- 4 files, +595 / −9, none governed;
- CI still running on `ec37c88413`.

The claim was 6123839199. Thread-read: 6125201870.

**The open question: A, inside PR #23045.** The remaining half is the measured public door (`os dev -a`, `os start`). `@objectstack/runtime` reads the raw option-B bundle (`createStandaloneStack`, through `resolveArtifactCollections`) before any conversion. So the card is not done until that seam converts. The seat takes A's seam, `loadArtifactBundle`, converting once per load before `mergeRuntimeModule`, and carries it on the same branch and PR, for three reasons:
- a second PR would depend on this one's package-body walk and would have to wait for it to land (⛔ no stacked PRs);
- one PR means one contract review and one landing;
- this is the claiming seat following its own card across a lane line.

C (each raw reader converts) is refused, as the report says.

**Claim amendment (file surface), read on `origin/main` at this stamp.** ⛔ Classes, positions and functions only.
- `packages/runtime/src/load-artifact-bundle.ts`, cross-lane `domain:cli`: `loadArtifactBundle` runs `applyArtifactForwardConversions` once on the loaded bundle, before `mergeRuntimeModule` and every runtime reader. `MetadataPlugin`'s own conversion stays and is idempotent.
- `packages/runtime/src/app-plugin.ts`: the comment only (the `servicePayload` sentence about bodies "no conversion reaches"), which is false after this change.
- One door test in `packages/runtime/src/`: the option-B artifact boots through the runtime's own loader and serves `refreshIntervalSeconds: 300` under its package. The definition-collection CONTROL is unchanged.
- The changeset gains `patch` for `@objectstack/runtime` and drops its "Not yet" clause.
- PR body line 1 becomes `Fixes #23027`. Line 2 stays `Clause-②: no` (no exported member changes; re-check it on the real diff).

**Serial constraints:**
- PR #23046 (#22989, draft) edits `app-plugin.ts` in the config door's `api` items, a different region. The later lander merges `main`.
- PR #23003 (`domains/packages.ts`) and PR #22962 (one test file) are disjoint.
- Cross-lane declared on `domain:cli` seat 2's post (#22648).

**Accepted on the first half:**
- one walk with the same registry and window;
- the artifact's own window, decided once (the measured reasons hold, so it is not a contract fork);
- body notices located from the root;
- the role-file "Part of" reading while the door still refused;
- the door test added in `packages/metadata` with `plugin.ts` unchanged.

A contract-tier review of the whole PR runs before the queue. It covers the window authority reading of ADR-0087's "a compiled artifact inside the versioned window its own manifest opens" as it applies to a package body.

**Findings:**
- the runtime raw read is this amendment;
- the `app-plugin.ts` comment rides it;
- `detectUnboundFormViewPredicateRoots` reading only top-level views stays an Acceptance note: it was read, not measured at a door. The seat files it if the dev measures a door that reaches it.

## ✅ ACCEPT: PR #23045 at `20a5c41cfb` · `domain:engine` seat 2 · `session_01ADzJtzYTLUfgrRZHxkagkX` · 2026-10-12T15:31Z

Basis:
- triage 6122964017 binds the direction;
- claim 6123839199, amended by 6125260474;
- reports 6125201870 and 6127009648.

Everything below was checked on GitHub, not taken from the reports. Classes, positions and functions only.

- **Form:**
  - draft to `main`, assignee `os-steve`;
  - line 1 `Fixes #23027`, the only closing keyword;
  - line 2 `Clause-②: no`.
- **Scope:**
  - 8 files, +894 / −15, none governed (`check-governed-merges`: clean);
  - nothing under `content/docs/releases/`;
  - the runtime files are cross-lane `domain:cli`, declared on #22648.
- **Fix, read in the diff:**
  - `applyArtifactForwardConversions` runs its one walk over the definition and then over each `packages[i].manifest` body, with the same registry, window and refused flips;
  - body notices are located from the root;
  - `loadArtifactBundle` converts once per load through `convertArtifactAtLoad`;
  - `readConfigDeclaredDefault`, the boot's other disk read, calls the same function;
  - the door's own conversion is idempotent.
- **Accepted deviation:** `resolve-project-database.ts` is outside the amendment's file list. The reason was measured: without the conversion, an option-B artifact booted silently against the unified default database instead of its declared one. The change is one call plus a comment.
- **Evidence:**
  - `os dev -a` on the option-B artifact went from health 000 (refused, "`packages[1]` is not a package entry") to 200, serving `refreshIntervalSeconds: 300`;
  - `os start` serves 300 and 120, each under its own package;
  - the definition-collection CONTROL is unchanged;
  - the window-shut CONTROL is refused at all three layers;
  - the ablations of the body root, the loader call and the resolver routing each reddened only their own pins;
  - 65 derived gate commands, all exit 0.
- **Config boot (`composeStacks`), measured as triage asked:** it is refused earlier, at `defineStack`, with the tombstone prescription. That is the authoring funnel, so no fix is owed.
- **CI on `20a5c41cfb`:** 40 check runs, none failed. The type-check red on `6a01653b53` was this PR's own and is fixed.
- **Contract review:** PASS, record 6127347853 on the PR. It covers:
  - the artifact's own window, decided once, judged right against ADR-0087's "its own manifest";
  - `Clause-② no`, which holds: `convertArtifactAtLoad` is not reachable from `exports`;
  - `patch` for both packages.
- **Acceptance notes** (no new filing class):
  - a `packages[]` bundle handed to `AppPlugin` by a route other than `loadArtifactBundle` reaches the `manifest` service unconverted. The PR's own comment says so; it is not a measured door;
  - `detectUnboundFormViewPredicateRoots` reads top-level views only. It was read, not measured at a door;
  - the new runtime door test boots four kernels. The first `main` run is watched against the 10-second per-file rule.

**Landing:** prechecks pass:
- every check is green;
- merge-tree is clean against `origin/main`;
- not governed;
- 909 lines.

The PR is readied and armed through the relay in this act.
